# Anime Face Generator with DCGAN

A TensorFlow based Deep Convolutional Generative Adversarial Network project that trains on anime face images and generates new anime style faces from random noise.

The project includes a custom image dataset loader, a DCGAN generator and discriminator, a training script that saves image samples and checkpoints, and a generation script that creates new images from trained generator weights.

## Project Overview

This project uses a GAN architecture with two neural networks:

* Generator: creates fake anime face images from random noise.
* Discriminator: tries to distinguish real anime face images from generated ones.

During training, both models improve together. The generator learns to create more realistic anime faces, while the discriminator becomes better at detecting fake images.

## Features

* Loads anime face images from a local dataset folder
* Resizes all images to 64 by 64 pixels
* Normalizes image pixels to the range from minus 1 to 1
* Builds a DCGAN style generator using transposed convolution layers
* Builds a discriminator using convolution layers
* Trains the GAN with Binary Cross Entropy loss
* Saves generated sample grids after every epoch
* Saves generator checkpoints after every epoch
* Saves a training loss graph
* Generates new anime face images from saved checkpoints

